2026-08-24T20:05:00Z	tried	what=a silent fetch failure that made the retry loop lie	config=sync_with_remote returned Ok(None) on a failed git fetch; git network calls now go through gitcmd::git_env, which supplies the forward proxy unless the environment already sets one; rebase uses --autostash	produced=a full bank under 'env -u https_proxy -u http_proxy' now commits, mirrors and pushes; origin/main == local HEAD at 3e3f22b3, with both other sessions' commits (992c438, 5fa72b8) ancestors of ours	claim=MEASURED	control=the negative arm is the run itself: stripping every proxy variable from the environment is the condition that used to fail silently, and it now succeeds. Before the fix the same command reported 'the remote kept moving' three times against a remote that had not moved	why=This is the project's signature bug INSIDE the harness written to catch it, and my retry loop turned a silent no-op into a confident false explanation — worse than the original failure, because it named a cause. Two lessons: a fetch that could not run is UNKNOWN and never 'nothing to do'; and a detached process inherits nothing, so any dependency on an exported variable works interactively and fails unattended.	node=117796
